  "text": "Solution 2 is wrong. Its claim that size 1 is impossible fails: the universe containing only the zero game is dead-ending, and its misère quotient is trivial with one element. So the answer is not 1.\n\nSolution 1 claims that 3 is the only non-realizable size, so its answer hinges on 5 being realizable. Its size-3 argument is also shaky. It relies on \"L + L = L\", which is not a valid partizan sum rule, and it does not really rule out other monoid structures. Its size ≥ 4 constructions are asserted, not shown.\n\nSolution 3 gives 3 and 5 as the non-realizable sizes, for a sum of 8. Its size-3 and size-5 arguments are also hand-waved, with no explicit verification shown. I cannot check this against the literature here, since I have no search tools. My recollection of the partizan misère quotient literature is that 3 and 5 are the exceptional orders, which matches Solution 3's answer, but that recollection is not reliable enough to be confident.\n\nOf the three, Solution 3 is the most likely to have the correct final answer. Its answer of 8 is my best guess, but it is unverified.\n\nCHOICE: 3",
